{"id": "97d32a70-2ef4-402d-a80d-1cd5713f968e", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check your CloudTrail trails and their data event selectors against the four resources. Trail configuration across regions and accounts can be large, so I'm running this check in the background.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_C6akOms1sy9YcrAaTO6aik", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "cloudtrail-data-event-coverage", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine which of the following resources currently have CloudTrail DATA EVENT logging captured by at least one active trail (or event data store), in account 012345678901, region us-east-1.",
  "resources": [
    "S3 bucket: nebula-audit-covered-012345678901",
    "S3 bucket: nebula-audit-uncovered-a-012345678901",
    "Lambda function: nebula-audit-fn-a (us-east-1)",
    "DynamoDB table: nebula-audit-table (us-east-1)"
  ],
  "context": "An audit requires data event logging on these four resources. The user wants to know which ones CloudTrail actually captures today. Be rigorous: list all trails (include shadow/organization trails and multi-region trails; use include_shadow_trails), check each trail's status (is it logging? IsLogging via get_trail_status), and read both basic event selectors and advanced event selectors (get_event_selectors). Also check CloudTrail Lake event data stores (list_event_data_stores / advanced selectors) if available. Correctly interpret: S3 selectors (AWS::S3::Object with ARN prefix matching, e.g. all buckets arn:aws:s3, or specific bucket ARNs; ReadWriteType Read/Write/All; excludeManagementEventSources and advanced field selectors such as resources.ARN with StartsWith/NotStartsWith/Equals, eventName filters, readOnly), Lambda selectors (AWS::Lambda::Function, all functions vs specific ARN), DynamoDB selectors (AWS::DynamoDB::Table, all vs specific ARN). Note any exclusions that would hide these resources, partial coverage (e.g. only Read or only Write events), and trails that are not logging or not multi-region. Also confirm the resources exist (head/describe) and capture the exact ARNs.",
  "criteria": "Return a per-resource verdict: COVERED (full read+write), PARTIALLY COVERED (explain), or NOT COVERED, naming the trail(s)/selector(s) that provide the coverage, and the evidence. If CloudTrail API calls via use_aws are blocked, use the lookup_cloudtrail_events route or other available means and clearly state any limitation on what you could verify. Do NOT make any mutating changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check CloudTrail data event coverage for four resources"}], "created_at": null}

